//【小太郎】
<voice name='小太郎' class='小太郎' src='voice/ma02/0110010b35'>
//「…………」
"......"

//【長坂】
<voice name='長坂' class='長坂' src='voice/ma02/0110020b45'>
//「どうよ。
//　小太郎……」
"Well?"

//【小太郎】
<voice name='小太郎' class='小太郎' src='voice/ma02/0110030b35'>
//「足跡が二つあるわ。
//　どうやら、誰ぞに拾われたようだの」
"Two sets of footprints. Someone carried him away."

//【長坂】
<voice name='長坂' class='長坂' src='voice/ma02/0110040b45'>
//「ほう……」
"Oh?"

//【小太郎】
<voice name='小太郎' class='小太郎' src='voice/ma02/0110050b35'>
//「心当たりはあろうかな。
//　このような場所を通りがかる者などに……」
"Do you have any idea who might have passed through these parts?"

//【長坂】
<voice name='長坂' class='長坂' src='voice/ma02/0110060b45'>
//「ある。
//　……あやつめが。全くいつまでも煩わしい
//男よ」
"Yes. ...That old fool. He never tires of getting in my way."

//【小太郎】
<voice name='小太郎' class='小太郎' src='voice/ma02/0110070b35'>
//「……」
"......"

//【長坂】
<voice name='長坂' class='長坂' src='voice/ma02/0110080b45'>
//「山に登るぞ。裏手へ回る」
"Let's go. It's on the other side of the mountain."

//【小太郎】
<voice name='小太郎' class='小太郎' src='voice/ma02/0110090b35'>
//「おいよ。
//　やれやれ……年寄りにはきついのう」
"As you wish. No rest for the ancient, I see."

//　<RUBY text='えみし'>蝦夷</RUBY>とは大和の少数民族を指す。
  The Emishi are an ethnic minority native to Yamato.

//　彼らは小規模の集団を作って全国各地に散在するが、
//全般的に見れば東北地方に近付くほど集団の規模・数
//ともに増大する。しかし他地方でも鍛冶の名地（美濃
//の<RUBY text='せき'>関</RUBY>村や備前の<RUBY text='おさふね'>長船</RUBY>村など）には集中して住む。
  They are located in small communities all over the country, but the closer you are to the Tohoku region, the more of them you will find. 

//　大和人と比べてやや小柄かつ細身の体格を持ち、肌
//は褐色、髪色は黒のほか白、銀、金などがみられる。
//　動きは俊敏で特に手先が器用であり、持久力に秀で、
//意外なほど筋力もあるが……
  Emishi are short and slender compared to the average Yamatoan, with dark skin and hair that can be black, white, silver, or gold. They are adept with their hands, nimble on their feet, and possess surprising strength relative to their slight frames.

//　生命力を欠くのか、病には弱く短命である。
//　平均寿命は三十数年程度、五〇年以上を生きる者は
//珍しい。
  However, they seem to lack a certain vitality. They are short-lived and prone to illness. The average life expectancy of an Emishi is thirty-odd years, with few living past fifty.

//　また彼らは特異な不老体質を備え、一五歳頃に成人
//を迎えて以後は死ぬまでほとんど容姿が変化しない。
  In addition, they have a peculiar quality of agelessness. Once an Emishi comes of age in their mid to late teens, their appearance changes very slowly thereafter.

//　東大和の先住民族として大和朝廷の歴史書に記述が
//現れる当初から劔冑鍛造を始めとする高度な鍛冶技術
//を有していたとされ、大和鍛冶の誕生は彼らとの接触
//が端緒であると通説は認める。
  Even in the earliest imperial histories, it is written that the Emishi possessed great skill in all manner of smithcraft: including, of course, the forging of tsurugi. Today, it is widely accepted that Yamatoan tsurugi-smithing was born out of contact with the Emishi.

//　中世以降、大和鍛冶と蝦夷鍛冶の間に技術的な格差
//はみられないが、種族的な適性の部分で差があるのか、
//一般に大和鍛冶の作品は蝦夷鍛冶のそれに及ばない。
  In general, Emishi craftsmen are superior to Yamatoan. Since any gap in technique was eliminated by the medieval period, it is likely that racial aptitudes are a factor.

//　そのため、蝦夷は少数民族の必然として偏見・蔑視
//を受けつつも、貴重な職能集団と扱われ、尊重されて、
//現在に至っている。
  As a result, Emishi have always been prized for their ability as tsurugi-smiths, even though they continue to suffer from the prejudices faced by most minority groups.

//　……一説によれば、彼らの短命と不老は鍛冶種族と
//して特化されているからこそだと云う。
//　蝦夷は心身と技術の成熟を迎えた時点で己を<RUBY text='ヨロイ'>甲鉄</RUBY>と
//するのが宿命。老境などという人生は必要ない、と。
  One theory holds that their short lifespan and agelessness are proof that evolution has adapted them to a life before the forge. When an Emishi reaches maturity and has mastered the art of smithing, they forge themselves into a tsurugi. With this fate all but ordained from birth, it is not necessary for them to live into old age.

//　大和国外にも同類と考えられる種族は複数存在し、
//西洋人類学はこれを総じて『<RUBY text='ドワーフ'>小さい人</RUBY>』と呼称する。
//　そのうち特に有名なものは白い肌の一種族であろう。
  Similar races are found all over the world. In the West, these are called dwarves. 

//　彼らは欧州全域に分布し、劔冑を始めとする武器の
//販売で巨富を築き、死の商人と、世界の黒幕と呼ばれ
//畏怖と嫌悪を集め――それが為に、
//　先の世界大戦においては最大の災厄を<RUBY text='こうむ'>蒙</RUBY>った。
  Of the dwarven races, the most famous are those known for their porcelain white skin.

  They spread throughout Europe during the middle ages, amassing great fortunes with their crafts. But because they specialized in the forging of weapons, they came to be feared as merchants of death. Many people even believed that they ruled the world from behind the scenes.

  Ultimately, this led to the horrific persecution of white dwarves during the last world war.

// 　彼らを称して<RUBY text='ユーデア'>賛美者の末裔</RUBY>。
//　大和語では白蝦夷と云う。
  In the West, they are known as Judea. In Yamato, we call them White Emishi.
